  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The definition of tags is too wishy washy about how to decide what to categorize it, I strongly a binary \"yes or no\" is not the answer, it would work better with a spectrum \"sliding scale\" like the ESRB or the Motion picture content rating system. Tags are not all or nothing and assigning an overall rating will deal with the systems, like tg\n\nGame Rating and Movie rating Systems that exist universally and are understood by an overwhelming majority of people.\n\nMy main intent is to reinforce that you can see what you want with a single button press:\n\n**\"G (for streamers and content creators), PG13 (default), Rated M (Everything), Custom (Per option choice)\"**\n\n>G is not really needed but it is good as a \"Safe Mode\" for streamers and content creators.\n\n>PG 13 being default for all VRC players.\n\n>Rated M being what the content should be filtered by default.\n\n>and Rated X will **not** be an option, rather, it is a way to explain to the user content that is prohibited or violates VRC's terms of service. (Pornographic, photorealistic or real Images of death, Illegal content, etc)\n\nThis will allow users to quickly understand what kind of content they are seeing and already have a familiarity of what should and should NOT be allowed. It can be localized to other countries with minimal effort by adjusting to local rating systems with a string change.\n\nThis also allows for faster categorization for streamer friendly content and the ability to whitelist avatars. Along with the ability for moderation to prioritize reported avatars that are untagged rather than tagged avatars, as less people will see them as the scale continues. \n\nThere can be Custom sliders to refine the content they see, such as the rating per content, similar to avatar safety settings.\n\n**In summary,** \n\nThe grading spectrum will allow for \n\nA. Users to understand the restraints immediately.\n\nB. Streamers to control the content they see.\n\nC. Allow Moderation to prioritize higher risk content and accelerate action.\n\nEDITED: Edited for Clarity\n\nAdded Sample (Sorry UI dev, it is cursed)\n\nQuick Settings and Full Settings",
